 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive Tier IV membership in the New York city teachers'\nretirement system to certain employees",
    "basePrintNo": "S8167",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8167-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8167\n\nSPONSOR: LANZA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act granting retroactive Tier IV membership in the New York city\nteachers' retirement system to certain employees\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant retroactive membership in the New York City Teach-\ners' Retirement System to certain employees\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one allows certain employees to file an application within one\nyear of this act taking effect for Tier IV status with the New York City\nTeachers' Retirement System.\n\nSection two states all past service cost associated with this act shall\nbe borne by the City of New York. Section three is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would allow certain employees, who were employed by the City\nof Yonkers Parks Department beginning in 2009 and ending in 2014 and who\nare now employed by the New York City Department of Education and are\nmembers of the New York City Teachers' Retirement System (NYC TRS) to\napply for retroactive Tier IV membership. This bill grants this benefit\nto certain employees, for reasons not ascribable to their own negli-\ngence. This bill would grant certain employees service credit in the NYC\nTRS for their employment with the city of Yonkers Parks Department for\nthe period beginning in 2009 and ending in 2014.  Additionally, the bill\ngrants these certain employees Tier IV status in NYC TRS, provided that\nan application is filed with the head of the NYC TRS within one year\nfrom the effective date of this act.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024: S.7520-B - Referred to Civil Service / A.7745-B - Referred to\nGovernmental Employees\n\n2023: Similar to S.7520 - Referred to Rules / A.7745 - Referred to\nGovernmental Employees\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note after section three of bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
